<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-for-gestational-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin for Gestational Diabetes" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with gestational diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-for-gestational-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If you have gestational diabetes, you can manage your blood glucose level by following a healthy eating plan and doing a moderate-intensity physical activity, such as brisk walking for 150 minutes, each week. If consuming healthy food and beverages and getting regular physical activity aren’t enough to keep your blood glucose level in your target range, a doctor will work with you and may recommend you take insulin. Insulin is safe to take while you are pregnant." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you have gestational diabetes, you can manage your blood glucose level by following a healthy eating plan and doing a moderate-intensity physical activity, such as brisk walking for 150 minutes, each week. If consuming healthy food and beverages and getting regular physical activity aren’t enough to keep your blood glucose level in your target range, a doctor will work with you and may recommend you take insulin. Insulin is safe to take while you are pregnant." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-insulin-medicines-treatments> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-for-type-1-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
